  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildife Without Borders-Critically Endangered Animals</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will address the main threats to the conservation of the Indonesia Slow Loris, illegal trade and habitat loss, by improving law enforcement capacity and awareness, and increasing public awareness of the primate to reduce demand for their trade. Specific activities include: (1) mitigating the illegal trade in Slow Lorises through improved law enforcement by conducting workshops at government offices, and supporting confiscation attempts by providing assistance in species identification and medical checks; (2) reducing the demand for trade in Slow Lorises by developing and implementing a social media campaign, conducting offline awareness campaigns in local communities, and conducting awareness-raising workshops in local communities; (3) creating a Slow Loris genetic database for conservation purposes; (4) reinforcing wild populations in Halimun-Salak National Park and Batutegi Protected Forest Reserve with rehabilitated Slow Lorises; (5) increasing knowledge of Javan Slow Loris ecology, behavior, and habitat requirements by monitoring wild Lorises and constructing 12 phenology plots to collect data from.</narrative>
  </description>
